Check permissions:

[Screenshot3.png]
Registry permissions for the should allow Administrators, and the user account Full Control. Incorrect permissions can stop Windows from loading the profile; resulting in a temporary profile login.




## Why It Happened & Why the Fix Worked
Windows creates a temporary profile when it cannot load the normal profile due to corruption. 
- Backing up data and creating a new profile restores access to the user’s files.
- Correcting registry entries and permissions ensures Windows can properly link the profile to the user account, preventing future errors.

> **Note:** This issue can overlap with “Apps Not Opening” since corrupted profiles may prevent applications from launching correctly. **Note:**
